ttsandsttp (1.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Multi-provider STT and TTS catalog (bundled providers.json)
    - Groq, OpenRouter, Qwen/DashScope and any OpenAI-compatible endpoint
      for both directions, plus custom OpenAI/DashScope providers
    - 9 STT models and 20 TTS models with per-model request limits,
      voice lists, response formats and instruction support
    - OpenAI-compatible STT (multipart) and TTS (/audio/speech) clients
      with response-format negotiation, PCM/WAV/MP3 decoding and chunking
  * Larger TOML configuration
    - [providers.<id>] sections with endpoint, key and timeout overrides
    - [api] is deprecated and migrated in memory to [providers.dashscope]
    - API keys are scoped per provider: systemd credentials, keyring,
      0600 file or environment variable
    - `set-key`/`del-key` accept an optional provider argument
  * Language is optional
    - Cloud STT auto-detects the language; the DBus language may be empty
    - Global [tts] fallback speaks any language; per-language [tts.<lang>]
      sections and [stt.<lang>] overrides remain available
  * TTS playback pipeline: text chunking, prefetching, retries, gapless
  * New CLI: `providers`, `models`, `bench-tts`; `bench-stt` gains
    --provider/--model
  * Local (sherpa) remains the default and works fully offline

 -- digit1024 <digit1024@example.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 07:46:03 +0100

ttsandsttp (1.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Cloud providers (Alibaba Cloud Model Studio / DashScope "Qwen")
    - Opt-in cloud Speech-to-Text (qwen3-asr-flash) via [stt] provider
    - Opt-in cloud Text-to-Speech (qwen3-tts-flash) with voice selection
    - New [api] section: region presets (singapore/beijing/custom),
      configurable base URL and key handling
  * Secure API key storage: systemd credentials, freedesktop Secret
    Service keyring, 0600 file, or env; keys are never stored in config
  * New CLI: set-key, del-key, voices, bench-stt (local vs cloud A/B)
  * Bundled Qwen-TTS voice catalogue and `voices` command
  * Local (sherpa) remains the default and works fully offline

 -- digit1024 <digit1024@example.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:37:10 +0200
